# Shell hooks must stay LF so `sh` can run them (a CRLF shebang breaks /bin/sh).
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Round-V byte-parity fixtures. These XML parts are lifted verbatim from a
# reference Office .docx and must be byte-identical to the original on every
# platform so the in-zip parity gate succeeds. The original Office bytes use
# CRLF line endings (7,643 bytes, SHA-256
# B2295D3198893D2C03F5E584C749A15751B798AEFDCD9BEE2889F13903D68CB2 for
# theme1_reference.xml). Without this rule git autocrlf normalises to LF on
# Linux/macOS checkouts (7,642 bytes), breaking both the pinned-length test
# and the actual docx parity.
crates/agentic-export/tests/fixtures/theme1_reference.xml binary

# ADR-0064 iter41 (2026-07-04): FHNW MT-Template fixtures embedded in the
# `agentic-thesis-template` crate. Same rationale as the theme1_reference.xml
# rule above — the hardcoded `size_matches_fixture` tests assert byte-lengths
# that were measured on a Windows checkout (CRLF). Without a binary rule,
# git autocrlf normalises to LF on Linux/macOS checkouts and every
# `size_matches_fixture` test fails by ~1 byte per line. Also the fhnw_logo
# PNG must not be text-processed.
crates/agentic-thesis-template/tests/fixtures/*.xml binary
crates/agentic-thesis-template/tests/fixtures/*.png binary
